# B-618: env-to-name-set skips non-string keys (e.g., integer 0).
# An env dict may have auto-indexed (integer) keys from positional entries.
# env-to-name-set must produce a name-set containing only string keys.
[
  env:      [name: "Alice"  count: 42  0: "skip-me"]
  name-set: [env-to-name-set env]
]
=== out
Dict({"env": Dict({"name": String("Alice"), "count": Int(42), 0: String("skip-me")}), "name-set": Dict({"name": Int(1), "count": Int(1)})})
